;; Conformance fixture: data-classification/derived-tree-fails-closed-no-frame
;;
;; Per Spec 015 §project-egress (the `:rf.observe/derived-tree` note) +
;; §Direct reads and fail-closed frame resolution, and EP-0025 / rf2-vl0jur
;; (ruled by Mike 2026-06-23): a `:rf.observe/derived-tree` record projected with
;; NO live governing frame FAILS CLOSED. The EP-0025 fail-open is scoped to a
;; re-keyed VALUE under a LIVE frame; an unresolvable / absent frame is the same
;; silent-leak risk every direct read carries off-box, so the whole tree redacts
;; to `:rf/redacted` rather than ship raw. This pins the rf2-vl0jur reconciliation
;; so a future port cannot re-absorb the retired raw-tree carve-out (a derived
;; tree must never ship raw on no live frame — it would leak any re-keyed secret
;; copied into the tree off-box).
;;
;; The four-case rule the framework upholds:
;;   1. live frame + declared path             -> redact/elide by path;
;;   2. live frame + re-keyed/undeclared pos    -> raw (EP-0025 fail-open);
;;   3. NO live frame + no explicit raw opt-in  -> FAIL CLOSED (:rf/redacted);  <-- pinned here
;;   4. explicit trusted-local raw opt-in       -> raw.
;;
;; Mode-B pure-call (`:project-egress`) with NO `:frame` key: the runner runs the
;; projection with `*current-frame*` bound to nil, so the call site is genuinely
;; frameless. The record carries `:frame nil`, so `project-egress`'s frame-seed
;; finds nothing and the derived-tree projector delegates to `elide-wire-value`'s
;; fail-closed path. The off-box-tool profile floors `:rf.size/include-sensitive?
;; false`, so the whole tree fails closed.
;;
;; Mirrors the unit-level `re-frame.projection-cljs-test/derived-tree-nil-frame-
;; fails-closed` (+ the unknown/destroyed/slot-keys siblings), lifted to the
;; host-agnostic corpus.

{:fixture/id           :data-classification/derived-tree-fails-closed-no-frame
 :fixture/spec-version "1.0"
 :fixture/capabilities #{:data-classification/classification-effects}
 :fixture/doc          "project-egress of a :rf.observe/derived-tree record with NO live frame fails closed — the whole tree redacts to :rf/redacted (rf2-vl0jur; the EP-0025 fail-open is scoped to a re-keyed value under a LIVE frame, not an unresolvable frame; the raw-tree carve-out is retired)."

 :fixture/calls
